Anchor Tags (<a>)
Syntax:
$$ \texttt{<a href="URL" target="_blank">Link Text</a>} $$
mailto: opens the default email client with the recipient filled.
tel: triggers phone dialer on compatible devices.
Always use full URLs with protocol (http:// or https://) to avoid broken links.
target="_blank" opens links in new tabs to improve usability.
Internal navigation via IDs enhances user experience by allowing quick jumps within the page.
Images (<img>, <picture>, <source>)
Basic image tag:
$$ \texttt{<img src="image.png" alt="Description" width="100" height="auto">} $$
Avoid spaces in filenames; use underscores or camelCase instead.
Use relative paths (./folder/image.png) or absolute paths depending on project structure.
Responsive images use:
<picture>
  <source srcset="image-small.png" media="(max-width: 650px)">
  <source srcset="image-large.png" media="(min-width: 651px)">
  <img src="image-default.png" alt="Description">
</picture>
​
This enables the browser to select the most appropriate image based on screen size.
Image Maps
Define clickable areas on images using coordinates with <map> and <area> tags.
Example coordinate shapes: rectangle, circle, polygon.
Allows different links or actions per region of the image.
JavaScript can be used for enhanced interactivity with click event handlers.
Commonly used in social media for tagging or interactive images.
